A classic, deeply savory beef stew cooked with carrots, celery, potatoes, condensed tomato soup, and mixed vegetables. Thickened with a classic butter-flour roux paste stirred in toward the end of cooking for a glossy, luscious gravy.

*Adapted from [Robert Irvine / Food Network](https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/robert-irvine/caribou-stew-recipe).*

## Ingredients

- 1 to 1.5 lbs stew beef (or venison/caribou), cut into bite-sized cubes
- 4 large carrots, peeled and medium-diced
- 1 large onion, peeled and medium-diced
- 1 stalk celery, scrubbed and medium-diced
- 1 lb potatoes, peeled and medium-diced
- 1 can (10.75 oz) condensed tomato soup
- 3 cloves garlic, finely minced
- 1 dried bay leaf
- 1 quart (4 cups) beef stock
- 2 tablespoons finely chopped fresh thyme leaves
- 1 teaspoon finely chopped fresh rosemary leaves
- 1 small package (approx. 10 to 12 oz) frozen peas, corn, or mixed vegetables
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- ½ cup all-purpose flour
- 4 oz (1 stick) unsalted butter, melted

## Instructions

1. **Combine Meat, Vegetables, and Broth:** Place the cubed beef, carrots, diced onion, celery, potatoes, condensed tomato soup, minced garlic, and bay leaf into a heavy Dutch oven or stockpot. Pour in the beef stock and stir to combine. Place over high heat until bubbling vigorously, then lower heat, cover tightly with the lid, and cook at a gentle simmer for 45 minutes.
2. **Prepare the Roux Paste:** In a small bowl, whisk the melted butter into the flour with a fork or small whisk until a smooth, lump-free paste forms.
3. **Incorporate Thickener, Herbs, and Frozen Veggies:** Whisk the butter-flour paste directly into the simmering stew, stirring steadily until completely dissolved into the broth. Fold in the fresh thyme, rosemary, frozen peas, corn, or mixed vegetables, salt, and black pepper.
4. **Simmer to a Rich Gravy:** Leave the pot uncovered and continue simmering over medium-low heat for 30 minutes, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking. The broth will thicken into a rich, velvety gravy while the meat and root vegetables become tender.
5. **Discard Bay Leaf and Serve:** Remove and discard the bay leaf. Taste the gravy and adjust salt and black pepper as desired. Ladle steaming bowlfuls accompanied by warm crusty bread or biscuits.

## Notes

- **Slow Cooker Instructions:** Place the beef, carrots, onion, celery, potatoes, condensed tomato soup, minced garlic, bay leaf, and beef stock into a 6-quart slow cooker. Cover and cook on LOW for 7 to 8 hours (or HIGH for 4 to 5 hours) until the meat is fork-tender. About 30 minutes before serving, whisk together the melted butter and flour into a paste. Stir the paste into the slow cooker along with the fresh thyme, rosemary, and frozen vegetables. Cover and cook on HIGH for the final 30 minutes until the gravy thickens and the vegetables are hot throughout.
- **Game Meats:** Venison, elk, or caribou make fantastic lean substitutions for beef in this stew.